# Pandoc Documentation Creator - Help

## Overview

This project provides a complete Pandoc-based documentation system with Docker support. It includes:

- Professional LaTeX templates
- Code syntax highlighting with VSCode Light theme
- PlantUML and Mermaid diagram support
- Automatic table of contents generation
- Configurable metadata and styling

## Quick Start

### 1. Initialize Your Project

Run the initialization script to create the project structure:

```bash
./init.sh new
```

This creates:
- `chapters/` - Your documentation chapters
- `media/` - Images and diagrams
- `output/` - Generated PDFs
- Default configuration files

### 2. Write Your Documentation

Edit markdown files in the `chapters/` directory:

```bash
chapters/
  01-introduction.md
  02-setup.md
  03-usage.md
```

### 3. Build Your PDF

```bash
./build-pdf.sh
```

Your PDF will be in `output/documentation.pdf`

## Project Structure

```
your-project/
├── chapters/           # Documentation chapters (markdown)
├── media/             # Images, diagrams, assets
├── output/            # Generated PDF output
├── metadata.yaml      # Document metadata (title, author, etc.)
└── build-pdf.sh       # Build script
```

## Configuration

The Pandoc defaults configuration is built into the Docker image. You only need to customize the document metadata.

### Metadata (metadata.yaml)

Configure document properties:

```yaml
title: "My Documentation"
author: "Your Name"
date: "2026"
lang: "en-US"
documentclass: scrartcl
papersize: a4
```

All Pandoc behavior (filters, templates, styling) is pre-configured in the Docker image. You only customize the document-specific metadata.

## Features

### Code Highlighting

Supports multiple languages with syntax highlighting:

````markdown
```python
def hello():
    print("Hello, World!")
```
````

### Diagrams

#### PlantUML

```plantuml
@startuml
Alice -> Bob: Hello
Bob -> Alice: Hi!
@enduml
```

#### Mermaid

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Start] --> B[Process]
    B --> C[End]
```

### Images

```markdown
![Caption](media/image.png)
```

### Tables

```markdown
| Header 1 | Header 2 |
|----------|----------|
| Cell 1   | Cell 2   |
```

### Blockquotes

```markdown
> This is a highlighted quote
```

## Advanced Usage

### Custom Build Options

Edit the build script to customize:

```bash
docker run --rm -v "$(pwd):/data" --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-documentation-creator:latest \
  -c "pandoc --defaults=/usr/local/share/pandoc/defaults.yaml --metadata-file=/data/metadata.yaml /data/chapters/*.md -o /data/output/documentation.pdf"
```

### Using Different Templates

Specify a different template:

```bash
--template=custom-template.tex
```

### Adding Filters

Add custom Pandoc filters in your defaults file:

```yaml
filters:
  - pandoc-plantuml
  - pandoc-mermaid-filter
```

## Docker Commands

### Pull the Image

```bash
docker pull registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-documentation-creator:latest
```

### Run Manually

```bash
docker run --rm -v $(pwd):/data --entrypoint=/bin/sh \
  registry.gitlab.com/woofi4/public/pandoc-documentation-creator:latest \
  -c "pandoc --defaults=/usr/local/share/pandoc/defaults.yaml --metadata-file=/data/metadata.yaml /data/chapters/*.md -o /data/output/documentation.pdf"
```

## Troubleshooting

### Docker Issues

- Ensure Docker is running: `docker ps`
- Check image exists: `docker images | grep pandoc`

### Build Errors

- Check file permissions: `ls -la chapters/`
- Verify markdown syntax in your files
- Check logs in terminal output

### Font Issues

- List available fonts: `fc-list`
- Modify font settings in metadata.yaml

